<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles II, Margrave of Baden-Durlach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1529">1529</a>–<a href="/years/1577">1577</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles II, Margrave of Baden-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durlach">Durlach</a>, ruled the margraviate from 1553 to 1577. He introduced the Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in 1556 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-augsburg">Peace of Augsburg</a> allowed princes to choose their territory's faith, and in 1565 moved his residence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pforzheim">Pforzheim</a> to Durlach, giving the margraviate its name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ii-margrave-of-baden-durlach.jpg" alt="Charles II, Margrave of Baden-Durlach" width="320" height="506" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_II._von_Baden-Durlach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
